# Python REST API backend based on FastAPI generated by Telosys $now.datetime 

${SHARP}${SHARP} Check prerequisites  
- Check that you have **Python** 3.10 or higher installed on your system.   
You can verify this by running: ```python --version```
If you don't have Python installed, you can download it from the official website: https://www.python.org/downloads/  
Optionally, you can set up a "virtual environment" to manage dependencies in the project folder.  
This is recommended to avoid conflicts with other Python projects on your system.
  - create a virtual environment:  ```python -m venv env```  (creates a folder 'venv' in the current directory)  
  - activate the virtual environment:  ```venv/Scripts/activate```    
   
- Check that you have **'pip'** (package installer for Python) installed.  
You can verify this by running: ```pip --version```
If you don't have pip installed, you can follow the instructions here: https://pip.pypa.io/en/stable/installation/  
Ensure that pip is up to date by running: ```pip install --upgrade pip```

- Install dependencies:
  - Install FastAPI and Pydantic v2 ('standard' for development) using pip:
    ```pip install "fastapi[standard]"```
  - Install SQLAlchemy (for database access) using pip:
    ```pip install sqlalchemy```
  - Install the database driver for the target database:
    - For PostgreSQL (psycopg v3):  ```pip install psycopg[binary]```
    - For SQLite: nothing to install (the driver is included in the standard Python distribution)

${SHARP}${SHARP} Run the application  
Start the development server:  
```fastapi dev main.py --port 8000```  
This will start the FastAPI development server on port 8000.   
You can access the API documentation at http://localhost:8000/docs

For production deployment, you can use Uvicorn:  
```uvicorn main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000```   
This will start the server on all available network interfaces on port 8000.
For help: ``` uvicorn --help```